WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- All right.

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:02.010
We are almost outta time, y'all

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.620
but let's squeeze in one more
inspiring story before we go.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.714
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:08.700
(rock music)

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.890
Middle school is a tough age.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:12.780
I hated middle school,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.570
which is why what I'm about
to share is truly special.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.340
A seventh grader noticed his classmate

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.870
was getting bullied for his appearance

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.550
and wanted to do something about it.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.890
So 12-year-old, Melo, decided he wanted

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.450
to give his classmate, Melvin,

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.790
a pair of sneakers to cheer him up.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.160
And he even offered to give
up his Christmas presents

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.390
and allowance to do so,

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.550
and Melo followed
through on his commitment.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.940
He even gave Melvin
the sneakers at school.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.290
The story would've ended there,

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.140
except the dean saw Melvin
actually carrying the box.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.560
And when he learned about this
story, he took this picture.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.750
Folks, this is what kindness looks like.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.130
We can be better humans.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.992
Let's pay attention to our youth.

00:00:48.992 --> 00:00:51.300
Melo and Melvin are with us right now.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.700
What's up, y'all?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.604
(audience cheering)

00:00:54.604 --> 00:00:56.550
- Hi.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.510
- What's up?

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.370
Melo, I'm gonna start with you.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.910
Like why was doing this
so important to you?

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.223
- Doing this was so important to me.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.400
When I saw Melvin getting bullied in class

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.000
it really hurt me in a way
because when I was younger

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.120
I got bullied because of my height.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.060
So I called my mom after school

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.980
and let her know how I was feeling

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.980
and how everything going on
with Melvin made me feel.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.110
And we went and got Melvin
a pair of shoes immediately

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.600
and then the next day I gave it to him.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.680
And I was happy to see
the reaction of Melvin

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.690
that he was so happy.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.160
- Oh my gosh, I love that.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.710
So Melvin, those are some
pretty cool kicks, man.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.480
You like your shoes?

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.160
- Yes, I love the shoes

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.910
and I'm very grateful for
what Melo did for me.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.360
I wish other kids could
be just like Melo

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.310
helping others out.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.143
- Absolutely.

00:01:57.143 --> 00:01:57.976
You're absolutely right.

00:01:57.976 --> 00:02:01.530
And not only by the way,
like Melvin, not only kids,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.880
but a grown adult.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.550
Like we can all learn a
lesson from this, you know?

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.450
It's a beautiful thing

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.710
to do something nice for someone

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.590
and it's also a lesson for
like all the bullies out there.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.170
Like stay on your own front porch.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.100
Quit worrying about ours.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.630
Anyway, thank you so much.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.136
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.820
(audience clapping)

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.940
And that's not all, you guys.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.710
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.320
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.990
want to honor inspiring
kids just like y'all.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.850
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.481
to each of you for $500.

00:02:32.481 --> 00:02:35.484
(audience cheering)

00:02:35.484 --> 00:02:36.933
- There's no way.

00:02:38.333 --> 00:02:39.166
Yes.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:41.400
- Thank you.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.140
- Oh my God, that was
the greatest reaction.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.583
Oh my God, Melvin.

00:02:49.884 --> 00:02:52.650
Melvin, you win for
greatest reaction ever.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.700
He left.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.170
He left the screen.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.240
He was like, bye.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.190
Oh my God, I love you guys.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.130
Keep being amazing humans, all right.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.500
And thank you to all our
guests today this hour.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.770
Kristin Chenoweth, Khris
Davis, Isaiah, Matchbox Twenty,

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.470
and a huge thank you to Jude and Isaiah

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.290
and my music director,
Jason Halbert, who I love.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.220
Have a great day, y'all.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.070
If it's not great, try and change it.

